Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: match NSS scheme allocation failure to uint8_t API

nss_wifili_thread_scheme_alloc() returns uint8_t. Its failure return of -1
therefore reaches the int caller as 255, not -1. Match the wire/API sentinel
so the existing fallback to scheme zero runs and failure is not marked as
a successful thread-scheme allocation. Valid scheme IDs are unchanged.

This fixes an allocation-failure path, not a demonstrated payload-starvation
cause. It does not change priorities, pool sizes or the driver ABI.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.h
@@ -124,7 +124,7 @@
 /* Enables the MCBC exception in NSS fw, 1 = enable */
 #define ATH11K_NSS_ENABLE_MCBC_EXC	1
 
-#define WIFILI_SCHEME_ID_INVALID	-1
+#define WIFILI_SCHEME_ID_INVALID	0xff
 
 enum ath11k_nss_opmode {
 	ATH11K_NSS_OPMODE_UNKNOWN,
